  /chats/{id}/group_tags:
    post:
      operationId: ChatMemberOperations_addTags
      description: >-
        Add tags


        Links tags to a conversation or a channel so that the chat membership keeps itself up to date.


        After adding a tag, all its members automatically become members of the chat. The tag and chat member lists are
        synchronized automatically: when a new member is added to the tag, they immediately appear in the chat; when
        removed from the tag, they are removed from the chat.


        If at least one of the tags passed is not found, the method responds `404` and links none of them. A tag already
        linked to the chat is not linked again, but its members are still pulled into the chat. A bot that may not be in
        tags does not come into the chat through a tag.


        A tag can be linked by a member of a private conversation and by any employee of the workspace in an open chat,
        while taking it off is available only to the chat owner or a chat administrator through the [Remove tag from
        chat](DELETE /chats/{id}/group_tags/{tag_id}) method. For a guest and a multi-guest the method responds `403`,
        whatever their role in the chat.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Chat ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 334
          example: 334
      responses:
        '204':
          description: 'There is no content to send for this request, but the headers may be useful. '
        '400':
          description: The server could not understand the request due to invalid syntax.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '422':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Members
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/AddTagsRequest'
      x-requirements:
        scope: chat_members:write
        roles:
          - owner
          - admin
          - user
          - bot
  /chats/{id}/group_tags/{tag_id}:
    delete:
      operationId: ChatMemberOperations_removeTag
      description: >-
        Remove tag from chat


        Unlinks a tag from a conversation or a channel and takes out the employees who were held there by it alone.


        The removal happens in the background, after the response: the method responds `204` immediately, and the chat
        membership changes a few moments later. The chat owner, those brought in by another tag of the same chat, and
        those added to the chat by hand will stay.


        A tag can be taken off a chat by the chat owner or a chat administrator. It can be linked back with the [Add
        tags](POST /chats/{id}/group_tags) method.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Chat ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 334
          example: 334
        - name: tag_id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Tag ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 86
          example: 86
      responses:
        '204':
          description: 'There is no content to send for this request, but the headers may be useful. '
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Members
      x-requirements:
        scope: chat_members:write
  /chats/{id}/leave:
    delete:
      operationId: ChatMemberOperations_leaveChat
      description: >-
        Leave chat


        The token owner leaves a conversation or a channel on their own. In a private conversation the others see a
        system message about the departure; in a public chat and in a channel they do not.


        You cannot leave if an employee is held in the chat by a linked tag: the method responds `403` until the tag is
        taken off the employee or off the chat. For a guest and a multi-guest the method also responds `403`, whatever
        their role in the chat. You cannot leave a thread or a direct message: for a thread the method responds `403`,
        for a direct message `400` with the `personal_chat` code. You can leave an archived chat, though.


        You can come back to a public chat on your own, and to a private one only if one of the members adds you back.
        Another employee is taken out by [Remove chat member](DELETE /chats/{id}/members/{user_id}).
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Chat ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 334
          example: 334
      responses:
        '204':
          description: 'There is no content to send for this request, but the headers may be useful. '
        '400':
          description: The server could not understand the request due to invalid syntax.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '422':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Members
      x-requirements:
        scope: chats:leave
  /chats/{id}/members:
    get:
      operationId: ChatMemberOperations_listMembers
      description: >-
        List chat members


        Who belongs to a conversation, a channel, or a thread. Bots come on equal terms with employees, with `bot:
        true`.


        The workspace owner can retrieve the member list of any chat in the workspace. Admins and bots can only retrieve
        the member list of chats they belong to (or that are public).


        Only active employees make it into the results: suspended ones do not come, although their membership is kept.
        The `role` field of a record is the employee's role in the workspace. The method does not return a member's role
        in the chat: who holds which is shown only by the `role` filter, one request per role.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Chat ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 334
          example: 334
        - name: role
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Role in the chat. In a channel the owner, admins and editors write, and a member there is a subscriber.
          schema:
            allOf:
              - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ChatMemberRoleFilter'
            default: all
          example: all
          explode: false
        - name: limit
          in: query
          required: false
          description: >-
            Number of records to return per request. An integer outside the allowed range is replaced with the nearest
            bound.
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            minimum: 1
            maximum: 50
            example: 1
            default: 50
          example: 1
          explode: false
        - name: cursor
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Pagination cursor (from `meta.paginate.next_page` or `meta.paginate.prev_page`)
          schema:
            type: string
            example: eyJpZCI6MTAsImRpciI6ImFzYyJ9
          example: eyJpZCI6MTAsImRpciI6ImFzYyJ9
          explode: false
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The request has succeeded.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required:
                  - data
                  - meta
                properties:
                  data:
                    type: array
                    items:
                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/User'
                  meta:
                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/PaginationMeta'
                description: Response wrapper with data and pagination
        '400':
          description: The server could not understand the request due to invalid syntax.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '422':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Members
      x-paginated: true
      x-requirements:
        scope: chat_members:read
    post:
      operationId: ChatMemberOperations_addMembers
      description: >-
        Add chat members


        Adds employees and bots to a conversation, a channel, or a thread. A bot is added the same way as an employee:
        its `id` in `member_ids`. In a channel it receives the editor role, and in a conversation it becomes an ordinary
        member — and only after that can it write there.


        Members are added by employees and bots. For a guest and a multi-guest the method responds `403`, as in the
        interface, whatever their role in the chat.


        The role in the chat is assigned at the moment of adding: the workspace owner and an administrator become chat
        administrators, everyone else becomes an ordinary member. After that the chat role is not recalculated by
        itself: promoting an employee in the workspace does not change their role where they already belong. To change a
        role, use the [Change member role](PUT /chats/{id}/members/{user_id}) method.


        Those who already belong to the chat are silently skipped by the method, and this is not treated as an error. An
        unknown or inactive ID, however, stops the whole request: the method responds `404` and lists such values, and
        nobody is added.


        A bot is added only by someone its "Who can add the bot to chats" setting allows — see [Bot
        settings](/guides/bots/settings#kto-mozhet-dobavlyat-bota-v-chaty). If `member_ids` contains a bot you are not
        allowed to add, the method adds nobody and responds `403` with the `bot_add_denied` code and the IDs of such
        bots in `value`. If the same request also has an unknown ID, the response is `404` with both errors.


        A bot with the "Restrict to a single chat" setting that already belongs to another conversation or channel is
        not added either: the response is `409` with the `single_chat_bot_occupied` code and the IDs of such bots in
        `value`, and nobody from the request is added. Such a bot can still be added to threads.


        Adding a whole department at once is more convenient with a tag — [Add tags](POST /chats/{id}/group_tags): then
        the chat membership is maintained by itself.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Chat ID (conversation, channel, or thread chat)
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 334
          example: 334
      responses:
        '204':
          description: 'There is no content to send for this request, but the headers may be useful. '
        '400':
          description: The server could not understand the request due to invalid syntax.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '409':
          description: The request conflicts with the current state of the server.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '422':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Members
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/AddMembersRequest'
      x-requirements:
        scope: chat_members:write
        roles:
          - owner
          - admin
          - user
          - bot
  /chats/{id}/members/{user_id}:
    delete:
      operationId: ChatMemberOperations_removeMember
      description: >-
        Remove chat member


        Removes an employee or a bot from a conversation, a channel, or a thread. A thread is addressed by its
        `chat_id`. In a private conversation the removed member loses access to the chat but stays in the threads they
        belonged to.


        An employee held in the chat by a linked tag cannot be removed with this method: the response will be
        successful, but the employee will stay in the chat. Take the tag off them with [Edit employee](PUT /users/{id})
        or unlink the tag from the chat with the [Remove tag from chat](DELETE /chats/{id}/group_tags/{tag_id}) method.


        The chat owner cannot be removed: the method responds `400` with the `cannot_kick_owner` code. The owner can
        only leave the chat on their own, with the [Leave chat](DELETE /chats/{id}/leave) method.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Chat ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 334
          example: 334
        - name: user_id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: User ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 186
          example: 186
      responses:
        '204':
          description: 'There is no content to send for this request, but the headers may be useful. '
        '400':
          description: The server could not understand the request due to invalid syntax.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Members
      x-requirements:
        scope: chat_members:write
    put:
      operationId: ChatMemberOperations_updateMemberRole
      description: >-
        Change member role


        Changes the role of a member of a conversation or a channel. A role in a chat is not tied to a role in the
        workspace: a regular employee can be a chat administrator, and a promotion in the workspace does not change
        roles in chats.


        The `editor` role exists only in channels. You cannot change your own role, nor the role of someone who is not
        in the chat, nor the chat owner's: the owner always has Admin privileges in the chat. Setting the same role
        again is treated as an error, not as a repeat.


        A refusal comes with status `400`, and the code names the reason: `not_applicable` — the `editor` role outside a
        channel, `self_update` — your own role, `owner_protected` — the chat owner's role, `already_assigned` — the
        member already has this role, `forbidden` — you may not change this role. For an employee who is not in the chat
        the method responds `404`.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Chat ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 334
          example: 334
        - name: user_id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: User ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 186
          example: 186
      responses:
        '204':
          description: 'There is no content to send for this request, but the headers may be useful. '
        '400':
          description: The server could not understand the request due to invalid syntax.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '422':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Members
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/UpdateMemberRoleRequest'
      x-requirements:
        scope: chat_members:write
  /chats/{id}/unarchive:
    put:
      operationId: ChatOperations_unarchiveChat
      description: >-
        Unarchive chat


        Brings a conversation or a channel back from the archive: the chat appears in the lists again, and it becomes
        possible to write into it again.


        On a chat that is not in the archive anyway the method responds with success.
      parameters:
