  /custom_properties:
    get:
      operationId: CommonOperations_listProperties
      description: >-
        List custom properties


        The schema of the workspace's custom properties: the ID, the name, and the type of each. Only employees and
        tasks have such properties, their sets are independent, and the `entity_type` parameter picks the one you need.
        The values come with the entity itself — in the employee's profile or in the task. The IDs from here are needed
        in order to set those values.


        Properties of the "File" and "Multiple choice" types are not available through the API and do not make it into
        the results. The basic profile fields — name, phone, email, department, tags — do not either: these are not
        custom properties.


        The set of properties is defined by the workspace administrator, who also renames and deletes them. That is why
        the list is worth re-reading before work: addressing a property that no longer exists returns an error.
      parameters:
        - name: entity_type
          in: query
          required: true
          description: Entity type
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/SearchEntityType'
            example: User
          example: User
          explode: false
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The request has succeeded.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required:
                  - data
                properties:
                  data:
                    type: array
                    items:
                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/CustomPropertyDefinition'
                description: Response wrapper with data
        '400':
          description: The server could not understand the request due to invalid syntax.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '422':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Custom Properties
      x-requirements:
        scope: custom_properties:read
  /direct_url:
    post:
      operationId: DirectUploadOperations_uploadFile
      description: >-
        Upload file


        The second step of the upload: the file itself goes to the storage as a `multipart/form-data` form. The form
        fields and the address are taken from the response of the [Get signature, key and other parameters](POST
        /uploads) method and passed as they are, in the same order, with the file as the last field.


        The request goes not to the Pachca API but straight to the storage, and `204` with no body comes back in
        response. After that the file is attached by passing its `key` in the `files` field — to [New message](POST
        /messages) or [New draft](POST /drafts), and when editing either of them. The file name in `name` must have the
        same extension as the `key`, otherwise the message will be rejected.
      parameters: []
      responses:
        '204':
          description: 'There is no content to send for this request, but the headers may be useful. '
      tags:
        - Files
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          multipart/form-data:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileUploadRequest'
      x-external-url: directUrl
      x-requirements:
        auth: false
  /drafts:
    post:
      operationId: DraftOperations_createDraft
      description: >-
        New draft


        Puts a draft into a conversation, a thread, or a direct message. In the Pachca interface it shows up in that
        chat's input box, where an employee finishes it and sends it. A scheduled message is created by this same
        method: with the `schedule` field the draft goes out by itself at the appointed time, without it the draft
        simply lies there. The method itself sends nothing: a draft is sent with [New message](POST /messages), passing
        it the draft's `content` and `parent_message_id`, and `key`, `name` and `file_type` of each file in `files`.
        Sending a message does not remove the draft: the Pachca app clears it by itself, while through the API it is
        removed with the [Delete draft](DELETE /drafts/{id}) method — otherwise the text stays in the input box.


        A draft is visible only to its author — neither the other party nor a workspace administrator sees it. A chat
        can hold only one ordinary draft. A repeated call responds `409` with the `already_exists` code and the ID of
        the existing one in `payload.draft_id`. That one is finished with the [Edit draft](PUT /drafts/{id}) method. A
        chat holds no more than 50 scheduled messages.


        For a thread, `entity_id` takes the ID of the thread itself, not of the message it hangs under. A direct message
        with an employee may not exist yet — then it is created by itself, the same way as when an ordinary message is
        sent.


        An empty draft cannot be created: either text or attachments are needed.


        The method is not available to bot tokens.
      parameters: []
      responses:
        '201':
          description: The request has succeeded and a new resource has been created as a result.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required:
                  - data
                properties:
                  data:
                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Draft'
                description: Response wrapper with data
        '400':
          description: The server could not understand the request due to invalid syntax.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '409':
          description: The request conflicts with the current state of the server.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '422':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Drafts
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/DraftCreateRequest'
      x-requirements:
        scope: drafts:write
    get:
      operationId: DraftOperations_listDrafts
      description: >-
        List drafts


        Your own drafts, newest first.


        By default only ordinary drafts are returned: scheduled ones have to be asked for with the `type` parameter. In
        the response they are told apart by the `schedule` field.


        The pair `entity_type` and `entity_id` narrows the results down to a single chat, thread, or direct message. If
        there is no such chat or it is not accessible, the method responds with an empty list rather than an error.
      parameters:
        - name: type
          in: query
          required: false
          description: 'What to return: `regular` — ordinary drafts, `scheduled` — scheduled messages, `all` — both'
          schema:
            allOf:
              - $ref: '#/components/schemas/DraftType'
            default: regular
          example: all
          explode: false
        - name: entity_type
          in: query
          required: false
          description: >-
            Chat type for filtering by a single chat. Specified together with `entity_id`: sending only one of the two
            returns `422`.
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/MessageEntityType'
            example: discussion
          example: discussion
          explode: false
        - name: entity_id
          in: query
          required: false
          description: ID of what is named in `entity_type`. Specified together with it.
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 334
          example: 334
          explode: false
        - name: limit
          in: query
          required: false
          description: >-
            Number of entities returned per request. An integer outside the allowed range is replaced with the nearest
            bound.
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            minimum: 1
            maximum: 50
            example: 25
            default: 50
          example: 25
          explode: false
        - name: cursor
          in: query
          required: false
          description: Pagination cursor (from `meta.paginate.next_page` or `meta.paginate.prev_page`)
          schema:
            type: string
            example: eyJpZCI6MTAsImRpciI6ImFzYyJ9
          example: eyJpZCI6MTAsImRpciI6ImFzYyJ9
          explode: false
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The request has succeeded.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required:
                  - data
                  - meta
                properties:
                  data:
                    type: array
                    items:
                      $ref: '#/components/schemas/Draft'
                  meta:
                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/PaginationMeta'
                description: Response wrapper with data and pagination
        '400':
          description: The server could not understand the request due to invalid syntax.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '422':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Drafts
      x-paginated: true
      x-requirements:
        scope: drafts:read
  /drafts/{id}:
    get:
      operationId: DraftOperations_getDraft
      description: |-
        Draft info

        The draft. For a scheduled message its schedule comes here too.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Draft ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 4821
          example: 4821
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The request has succeeded.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required:
                  - data
                properties:
                  data:
                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Draft'
                description: Response wrapper with data
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Drafts
      x-requirements:
        scope: drafts:read
    put:
      operationId: DraftOperations_updateDraft
      description: >-
        Edit draft


        Changes your own draft: the text, the attachments, the schedule, and the message it will reply to
        (`parent_message_id`). Only the fields you pass are overwritten, so the text can be finished with `content`
        alone, without touching the attachments.


        An ordinary draft turns into a scheduled message if `schedule` is passed. The reverse transition is forbidden:
        `schedule: null` on a scheduled message responds `422` with the `draft_type_change_forbidden` code. To cancel
        the sending, the draft is removed with the [Delete draft](DELETE /drafts/{id}) method.


        Editing works only while writing into the chat is allowed. If access to the chat has been lost, editing responds
        `403`, while deletion works all the same.


        The draft's chat is not changed by this method, it does not accept `entity_type` and `entity_id`. To move a
        draft to another chat, create a new one and delete the old one.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Draft ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 4821
          example: 4821
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The request has succeeded.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required:
                  - data
                properties:
                  data:
                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Draft'
                description: Response wrapper with data
        '400':
          description: The server could not understand the request due to invalid syntax.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '422':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Drafts
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/DraftUpdateRequest'
      x-requirements:
        scope: drafts:write
    delete:
      operationId: DraftOperations_deleteDraft
      description: >-
        Delete draft


        Removes your own draft for good: it cannot be restored, and the attachments are deleted along with it. For a
        scheduled message deleting is the cancellation of the sending.


        It works even if writing into the chat is no longer possible. A repeated call responds `404`.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Draft ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 4821
          example: 4821
      responses:
        '204':
          description: 'There is no content to send for this request, but the headers may be useful. '
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Drafts
      x-requirements:
        scope: drafts:write
  /files/{id}:
    get:
      operationId: FileOperations_downloadFile
      description: >-
        Download file


        Returns the file itself, not a link to it, and works for any attachment the token can see. For attachments
        without a direct storage link it is the only way: their `url` field holds the address of this method, and it can
        only be opened with a token. Encrypted files and files sent from the workspace secure perimeter are served this
        way — both settings are covered in [Encryption and the secure perimeter](/guides/data-protection).


        A refusal comes as `403` with the `confidential_download_denied` code. The address being checked is the one the
        request came from, that is the address of your server, not of the employee whose token you use: for a server
        integration that is the most common reason to be refused.


        The response is the body of the file and a `Content-Disposition` header with its name, not `JSON`. An encrypted
        file is decrypted on the fly and comes as a whole attachment: `target` does not apply to it. If it could not be
        decrypted, the answer is `400` with the `decryption_failed` code.


        An attachment of a message is available to whoever sees the message itself, and an attachment of a draft only to
        its author.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: File ID from the attachment's `id` field
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 3560
          example: 3560
        - name: target
          in: query
          required: false
          description: >-
            What to return instead of the original file: `pdf_preview` — the document converted to PDF, `pdf_first_page`
            — the first page as an image, `thumb` — a scaled-down copy of the image, `image` — the image as it is.
            Without the parameter the original file comes. A variant this file does not have leads to `400`.
          schema:
            $ref: '#/components/schemas/FileTarget'
            example: thumb
          example: thumb
          explode: false
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The request has succeeded.
          content:
            application/octet-stream:
              schema:
                type: string
                format: binary
        '400':
          description: The server could not understand the request due to invalid syntax.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Files
      x-requirements:
        scope: files:read
  /group_tags:
    post:
      operationId: GroupTagOperations_createTag
      description: >-
        New tag


        Creates a tag. A tag is a way to keep chat membership up to date by itself: it is linked to a conversation or a
        channel, and everyone who has this tag ends up there automatically.


        Employees are added to a tag not here but in each employee's profile — [Edit employee](PUT /users/{id}) with the
        `list_tags` field. A fresh tag is created empty, with `users_count: 0`. It is linked to a chat by [Add
        tags](POST /chats/{id}/group_tags).


        The name is unique within the workspace, case-insensitively, and cannot contain `@`. A name already taken
        responds `400` with the `taken` code, and `409` comes only if the same tag was created at the same moment as the
        request. Tags can be created by the workspace owner and an administrator; the method is not available to a bot.
      parameters: []
      responses:
        '201':
          description: The request has succeeded and a new resource has been created as a result.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required:
                  - data
                properties:
                  data:
