                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Messages
      x-requirements:
        scope: messages:read
    put:
      operationId: MessageOperations_updateMessage
      description: >-
        Edit message


        Changes the text, files, and buttons of a message that has already been sent. In the interface it gets an edited
        mark. The text follows the same formatting rules as in the [New message](POST /messages) method.


        You can edit only your own messages, and only ordinary ones: a system, a forwarded, and a voice message are not
        changed by the method. There are no restrictions on how long ago the message was sent.


        Files and buttons are replaced as a whole: an empty array removes all of them, while the absence of the field in
        the body leaves them as they were. Any edit removes the link previews, and they are not built again.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Message ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 194275
          example: 194275
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The request has succeeded.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required:
                  - data
                properties:
                  data:
                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/Message'
                description: Response wrapper with data
        '400':
          description: The server could not understand the request due to invalid syntax.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '422':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Messages
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/MessageUpdateRequest'
      x-requirements:
        scope: messages:update
    delete:
      operationId: MessageOperations_deleteMessage
      description: >-
        Delete message


        Message deletion is available to the sender, admins, and editors in the chat. In direct messages, both users are
        editors. There are no time restrictions on message deletion.


        The text, files, and reactions disappear for everyone and are not restored, the pin is removed, and a "Message
        deleted" note stays in place of the message in the chat.


        The thread created under this message stays, together with all the messages inside it. For a message that is
        already deleted the method responds `403`, and whether it is deleted is shown by the `deleted_at` field in the
        response of [Message info](GET /messages/{id}).
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Message ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 194275
          example: 194275
      responses:
        '204':
          description: 'There is no content to send for this request, but the headers may be useful. '
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Messages
      x-requirements:
        scope: messages:delete
  /messages/{id}/link_previews:
    post:
      operationId: LinkPreviewOperations_unfurl
      description: >-
        Unfurl (link previews)


        Inserts into a message a link preview assembled by the bot itself: a title, a description, and an image. This
        way the company's internal addresses, which Pachca cannot open on its own, are shown in the chat as a card.


        The method is available only to a bot whose outgoing webhook is configured for link previews. Such a bot
        receives the `message_link_shared` event and answers it with this method, and it does not need to belong to the
        chat with the message — it is enough that the chat is in its workspace.


        The domain of the link must be in the bot's list of allowed ones, and the link itself must be present in the
        message text, otherwise the method responds with an error. The response comes back empty even when no preview
        has been applied. The message object does not carry previews: they are seen only in the app.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Message ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 194275
          example: 194275
      responses:
        '204':
          description: 'There is no content to send for this request, but the headers may be useful. '
        '400':
          description: The server could not understand the request due to invalid syntax.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '422':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Messages
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/LinkPreviewsRequest'
      x-requirements:
        scope: link_previews:write
        roles:
          - bot
  /messages/{id}/pin:
    post:
      operationId: MessageOperations_pinMessage
      description: >-
        Pin message


        Pins a message in the header of a conversation or a channel, where all members see it. There is no limit on the
        number of pinned messages.


        In threads the method does not work. A message that is already pinned responds `409`, and a deleted one `422`.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: Message ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 194275
          example: 194275
      responses:
        '204':
          description: 'There is no content to send for this request, but the headers may be useful. '
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
