  /users/{id}:
    get:
      operationId: UserOperations_getUser
      description: >-
        Employee info


        The employee's profile.


        A suspended employee is returned with `suspended: true`, a deleted one as `404`, like a non-existent one. A bot
        also comes here as an employee, with `bot: true`.


        For a multi-guest the method returns only those who come to them in [List employees](GET /users), and responds
        `404` for the rest.


        Email and phone come back as `null` if the display of personal data is turned off in the workspace and the
        caller is not an administrator. For a multi-guest they always come back as `null`. An employee sees their own
        profile in full — the same one is returned by the [Own profile](GET /profile) method, and without the
        `users:read` scope.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: >-
            User ID. In a web app link it is the number from the `user_id` parameter. The `profile_id` and `user-id`
            parameters name the employee the link was sent to.
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 12
          example: 12
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The request has succeeded.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required:
                  - data
                properties:
                  data:
                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/User'
                description: Response wrapper with data
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Users
      x-requirements:
        scope: users:read
    put:
      operationId: UserOperations_updateUser
      description: >-
        Edit employee


        Changes the employee's profile: only the fields you pass are overwritten. Custom property IDs are returned by
        [List custom properties](GET /custom_properties).


        The request is applied as a whole: if any field fails validation, for example the new `email` is already taken,
        nothing changes. Changing the email sends letters to the old and the new address. In a free workspace they count
        towards the same daily limit as invitations from [New employee](POST /users), and beyond it the response is
        `422` with the `daily_invites_limit` code.


        The `list_tags` field replaces the whole set of tags, so send the tags that are being kept along with the new
        one. A removed tag takes the employee out of the chats this tag brought them into, and a name that does not
        exist in the workspace yet creates a new tag together with the assignment.


        `suspended: true` suspends the employee: they lose access but remain in chats, tags, and tasks, while
        `suspended: false` brings them back. An employee is removed for good by [Delete employee](DELETE /users/{id}).


        The workspace owner can be edited only by themselves, and their role can be changed only to administrator.
        Turning a regular employee into a guest is impossible — in both cases the response is `403`.


        An unknown role value is silently ignored by the method: the response is successful and the role stays as it
        was.


        For a bot the method changes only the name (`first_name`), nickname, tags and `suspended`, and skips the other
        fields in the request. Which nickname and which tags a bot can be given is said at the `nickname` and
        `list_tags` fields. If the bot's settings changed during the request, the `422` response comes with the
        `bot_changed_concurrently` code: retry the request.


        The employee's avatar is set and removed by separate methods, [Upload employee avatar](PUT
        /users/{user_id}/avatar) and [Delete employee avatar](DELETE /users/{user_id}/avatar).
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: User ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 12
          example: 12
      responses:
        '200':
          description: The request has succeeded.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                type: object
                required:
                  - data
                properties:
                  data:
                    $ref: '#/components/schemas/User'
                description: Response wrapper with data
        '400':
          description: The server could not understand the request due to invalid syntax.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '409':
          description: The request conflicts with the current state of the server.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '422':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Users
      requestBody:
        required: true
        content:
          application/json:
            schema:
              $ref: '#/components/schemas/UserUpdateRequest'
      x-requirements:
        scope: users:update
    delete:
      operationId: UserOperations_deleteUser
      description: >-
        Delete employee


        Removes an employee from the workspace. This cannot be undone: they can be brought back only with a new
        invitation, and that will already be a different employee.


        What happens: they leave all conversations and channels except direct messages, all tags are taken off them, the
        tasks where they were the only assignee are deleted, and they are removed from the remaining ones. The messages
        and files they wrote stay in place.


        The workspace owner cannot be deleted — the method responds `403`. A repeated call responds `404`: the method no
        longer finds a deleted employee.


        If the employee is going on vacation or the dismissal is not final yet, use [Edit employee](PUT /users/{id})
        with `suspended: true`. Suspension is reversible and keeps chats, tags, and tasks.
      parameters:
        - name: id
          in: path
          required: true
          description: User ID
          schema:
            type: integer
            format: int32
            example: 12
          example: 12
      responses:
        '204':
          description: 'There is no content to send for this request, but the headers may be useful. '
        '401':
          description: Access is unauthorized.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '402':
          description: Client error
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
        '403':
          description: Access is forbidden.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                anyOf:
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
                  - $ref: '#/components/schemas/OAuthError'
        '404':
          description: The server cannot find the requested resource.
          content:
            application/json:
              schema:
                $ref: '#/components/schemas/ApiError'
      tags:
        - Users
      x-requirements:
        scope: users:delete
  /users/{user_id}/avatar:
    put:
      operationId: UserAvatarOperations_updateUserAvatar
      description: >-
        Upload employee avatar


        Sets or replaces the avatar of another employee. Available to the workspace owner and an administrator; not to a
        bot. The workspace owner's avatar can be changed only by themselves.


        The file is sent in `multipart/form-data` format, and the response contains only a link to the new image. `jpg`,
        `jpeg`, `png`, and `gif` are accepted, an animated `gif` must be no larger than 2 MB, and the image is scaled
        down to 1024 by 1024 pixels.


        Your own avatar is set by the [Upload own avatar](PUT /profile/avatar) method — it is available to all roles and
        to bots.
