      x-requirements:
        scope: user_status:read
    put:
      operationId: UserStatusOperations_updateUserStatus
      description: >-
        New employee status


        Sets a status for another employee — for example, "on vacation" for the time of their absence. Available to the
        workspace owner and an administrator; not to a bot, even with the scope.


        This same method turns on away mode for that employee with the `is_away` flag and sets the `away_message` text
        that anyone reaching out to them will see.


        The status is seen by everyone who sees the employee in the workspace. Only the fields you pass are overwritten,
        so someone else's status can be extended with `expires_at` alone.


        An expiry named in words is `expires_at`, not a part of the caption, and it is counted in the time zone of the
        employee the status is set for.


        The emoji and the caption are required only when there is no status yet. The emoji must be exactly one, with no
        text around it, and the caption no longer than 50 characters.


        Your own status is set by the [New own status](PUT /profile/status) method — it is available to all roles and to
        bots.
